  "response_text": "The stack pool is a block of reserved memory in RAM that stores the stacks for all threads in our OS. This is needed because a every thread needs it own stack to store local variables, function call information, and register values during context switching. However, since RAM is limited we need to carve out a dedicated chunk of memory, which is the stack pool, to manage all the threads in one place.\\nIn the future, when multiple threads exist in our OS, for every new thread created the kernel allocates a slice of the stack pool to become that thread\u2019s personal stack.\\n",
